menu "Network MIDI 2.0 (UMP over UDP)"

    config MIDI2_NET_RETX_RING
        int "Retransmit/FEC ring depth (UMP Data commands per session)"
        range 2 64
        default 16
        help
            Number of recently sent UMP Data commands retained per session for
            Forward Error Correction and to answer Retransmit Requests. Each
            slot costs MIDI2_NET_RETX_MAX_WORDS*4 + a few bytes.

    config MIDI2_NET_RETX_MAX_WORDS
        int "Max 32-bit words retained per UMP Data command"
        range 4 64
        default 16
        help
            UMP Data commands larger than this are not kept in the retransmit
            ring (a Retransmit Request for them yields a Retransmit Error).
            16 words covers any single channel-voice/SysEx7 message comfortably.

    config MIDI2_NET_TX_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Outgoing UMP queue depth"
        range 1 128
        default 16
        help
            Depth of the queue between the application and the transport task.
            When full, midi2_net_host_send_ump() drops (UDP semantics).

endmenu
